  "long_biography": {
    "plain_text": "Kul Rattan Chadha’s hotel idea grew from the travel needs of his fashion employees: design mattered to them, but their budgets limited their choices. With citizenM, he pursued a combination of comfort and affordability. Compact bedrooms, good beds and generous shared spaces put spending into the parts of a stay that guests would use most.\n\nHis interest in visual culture extends beyond business. Working with curator Liesbeth Willems, Chadha developed a contemporary art collection spanning paintings, sculpture, installations and video. Kunsthal Rotterdam presented a selection in its exhibition Trouble in Paradise, exploring human vulnerability and social tensions. The collection grew from occasional purchases into a sustained engagement with artists and new media.",
